   "description": "Exposure response was measured by comparing the change in sleep efficiencies of VEC-162 and placebo treated subjects upon a sleep schedule phase advance. Sleep efficiency (total time asleep divided by the time allowed as an opportunity for sleep in a period multiplied by 100%, where time allowed for sleep was 8 hours or 480 minutes) was measured objectively by overnight polysomnographic recordings. Sleep efficiency was also compared in parts of the night by dividing the full night into thirds.",
